<title>INDIA: India gives phone numbers for crash information.</title>
<headline>India gives phone numbers for crash information.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India has set up an emergency control room to provide information to people who believe family members may have been killed in the mid-air collision near New Delhi, airport officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>An estimated 350 people were killed on Tuesday when a Saudi Arabian Airlines Boeing 747 collided with a Kazakh Illyushin Il-76, about 80 km (50 miles) southwest of New Delhi.</p>
<p>The control room at New Delhi airport can be reached by dialling 91-11-548-1219 or 91-11-548-4052.</p>
</text>
